  "behavior": [
    "FailureText retains the original bytes through first NUL, sharing their storage on copy and assignment. UTF-8 text accessors and Display are presentation views; byte getters and print_to preserve original bytes.",
    "Base copy construction now supports the prior native-only 0xff case, retains Standard_Failure identity and excludes derived private buffer storage.",
    "OutOfMemory byte constructor/setter preserve native first-NUL and 1023-byte truncation semantics, with copies unchanged after replacing the source buffer.",
    "Stream insertion returns the original Rust writer; byte printing propagates Rust I/O errors."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The native probe includes padded ostream output and pre-set badbit as native-only diagnostics. Generic Rust Write does not implement these C++ stream state semantics, so Print and operator<< stay partial.",
    "Native OutOfMemory stores its message in an embedded fixed buffer to avoid allocating while reporting memory exhaustion. Rust Arc buffer creation/replacement allocates, so its constructor/setter stay partial despite matching byte contents.",
    "The base-assignment safe-borrow self-alias limitation remains separately recorded.",
    "Supplemental tests and native diagnostics do not add original legacy declarations."
  ],
